[6.1,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[2J   › what can larecode do?\n\n   Lare Code is a terminal coding agent that runs every tool call through a\n   permission policy.\n\n   - Works with any OpenAI-compatible provider\n   - Reads, edits, and searches your files with git checkpoints\n   - Skills, subagents, and MCP servers extend it\n   - Everything runs locally, no telemetry\n\n\n\n   ▣ Plan · demo-model\n\n\n\n\n┃\n┃  Ask anything… \"Fix a TODO in the codebase\"\n┃\n┃  Plan · demo-model\n╹▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀\n  ⠇ esc interrupt                                 tab agents  ctrl+p commands\n\n"]
[7.6,"o","\u001b[H\u001b[2J   Lare Code is a terminal coding agent that runs every tool call through a\n   permission policy.\n\n   - Works with any OpenAI-compatible provider\n   - Reads, edits, and searches your files with git checkpoints\n   - Skills, subagents, and MCP servers extend it\n   - Everything runs locally, no telemetry\n\n   Start with:\n\n   ```bash\n   larecode setup\n\n\n   ▣ Plan · demo-model\n\n\n┃\n┃  Ask anything… \"Fix a TODO in the codebase\"\n┃\n┃  Plan · demo-model\n╹▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀▀\n  ⠙ esc interrupt                                 tab agents  ctrl+p commands\n\n"]
